---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy" description="What EV Trip Reports collects and how it is used.">
  <section class="band band--tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="note" style="margin-top:20px">Draft, last updated October 16, 2026. Pending legal review.</p>

      <h2>Reading the guides</h2>
      <p>You can read every guide without an account.</p>
      <p>Tinylytics (tinylytics.app) counts visits. Their documentation says a visit record keeps the page address, the referrer when the browser sends one, the country, and a shortened browser string. We have not confirmed whether that script sets a cookie.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics counts visits too. Its beacon loads from static.cloudflareinsights.com.</p>
      <p>The typeface is Geist, served from this site, so no font request goes to a third party.</p>

      <h2>Requesting a plan</h2>
      <p>When you request a plan, we collect what you put in the form: your name, email, car, charge port and adapter, route, dates, passengers, memberships, and notes. We use those details to build your plan and to email it to you. The details are stored with our hosting provider, Cloudflare.</p>
      <p>Cloudflare Turnstile is on for this form. It checks that a person sent the request.</p>
      <p>AI tools help research and draft plans, so your trip details may be processed by an AI provider for that purpose. We don't use your details for anything else.</p>

      <h2>Finding a plan</h2>
      <p>An approved plan is on a private link. We store a hash of that link, not the link itself. Find my plans emails a one-time link to the address you used at checkout. That link expires in 15 minutes and works once. We store a hash of it, that email address, the time it was sent, and the time it was used. The same Turnstile check runs on that form. The page does not say whether an email has a plan.</p>

      <h2>Newsletter</h2>
      <p>Signup is closed. If we open it, the form sends your email to Buttondown. Buttondown stores it and sends the updates after you confirm. You can unsubscribe from any of those emails.</p>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't sell or rent your information.</li>
        <li>We don't share it with charging networks, hotels, or advertisers.</li>
        <li>We don't add you to the newsletter unless you ask.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>Ask us to delete your request and its details at any time by replying to any email from us, or write to <a href="mailto:admin@evtripreports.com">admin@evtripreports.com</a>. We delete plan requests one year after the trip date unless you ask us to keep them.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top will change with it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
